WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.691
For the first practice task, create three simple panels on DrawSplat.

2
00:00:04.891 --> 00:00:09.107
The first asks for a prediction about the best location for a plant.

3
00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:12.564
The second asks learners to record observations.

4
00:00:12.764 --> 00:00:16.433
The third asks them to revise or defend the prediction.

5
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:19.666
Use text, a sketch or a supplied image.

6
00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:25.998
Keep the question visible and avoid filling the board with instructions that compete for attention.

7
00:00:26.198 --> 00:00:31.738
Model the reasoning with a different example so that students still have a new decision to make.

8
00:00:31.938 --> 00:00:36.701
State the claim, point to the observation and explain the connection.

9
00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:41.654
Ask a learner to restate the reasoning rather than repeat the sentence word for word.

10
00:00:41.854 --> 00:00:45.362
Your model should make the hidden decision process visible.

11
00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:49.403
Then leave part of the next example for the learner to complete.

12
00:00:49.603 --> 00:00:54.827
Before calling the launch ready, check that each panel requires thinking you can assess.

13
00:00:55.027 --> 00:00:57.449
Save and reopen the editable board.

14
00:00:57.649 --> 00:01:03.078
Plan to collect a brief individual explanation even if students discuss in pairs.

15
00:01:03.278 --> 00:01:07.365
A colleague should be able to teach the launch from your one-page plan.

16
00:01:07.565 --> 00:01:12.861
Pause and finish your three panels, two criteria, saving routine and fallback.

17
00:01:13.061 --> 00:01:16.549
You will develop this same lesson through the remaining modules.

